      {
        "id": 176014,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-05-29T00:00:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Only comics I've read are Watchmen, V for Vendetta, and Sandman, so I'm also not really a comics-reader.</p>\n<p>I'd definitely suggest Watchmen. If you've seen the movie first, though, it may lose some punch because the movie is almost a frame-by-frame remake of the comic. Yet, somehow, it's not as good.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Reading the comic afterward was definitely the right choice, because yeah, the movie's not that great.</p>\n<p>V for Vendetta meanwhile is one of my all-time favorite movies, and when you read the comic, it gives the story a lot more subtext. That one, I enjoy two different ways.</p>",
